# Copy to .env and fill in. `.env` is gitignored — never commit the real file.
#
#   cp video/.env.example video/.env
#   $EDITOR video/.env
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY — OPTIONAL. You do not need this to edit video.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transcription has two routes and the free one is the default:
#
#   Local Whisper (default)  no key, no cost, runs offline. Good word timings.
#   ElevenLabs Scribe        needs this key, costs credits. Adds speaker
#                            diarization and audio-event tags — (laughter),
#                            (applause), (sigh).
#
# Single talking head  → skip this entirely, local Whisper is fine.
# Multi-speaker interview or podcast → the key pays for itself in not
# hand-labelling who said what.
#
# Get one at https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where this file is read from
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# video-use looks in two places, in order:
#   1. <video-use repo>/.env
#   2. ./.env  (the directory you launched the agent from)
#
# `bash video/setup.sh` links this file into the video-use repo root, so
# keeping the key here means it survives re-cloning the tool repos.
#
# An exported ELEVENLABS_API_KEY in your shell overrides both.
